==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Terun, type ζ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Terun ζ''' at level 30 by using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Terun is an average generalist but a fairly good specialist. Her most prominent feature is her uptime against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, which goes up to a near perma-slow assuming the [[Blood Fruit]] and [[Enigma Fruit]] have been maxed out.

Early in the game, Terun can be used as a better [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], though the majority of [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] in the game can serve that purpose as well. However, she stands out among other Uber Rares due to her low cost (3,000¢) and very good recharge time (~62 seconds). With this, low DPS is no longer a problem as it can be accumulated overtime. Past mid-game however, she falls off in comparison. Her 35k health and below-average DPS are only enough to just make a dent, although this is somewhat compensated with her short recharge time and cost. If you're really striving for a generalist in the later stages of the game, use [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]].

Now onto her other abilities. Her Colossus Slayer isn't especially helpful, as you'll most likely already have a good specialist against their respective traits. Not to mention she gets outranged by the majority of [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus Enemies]], making the ability nearly useless against most of them. [[Baron Seal]], however, is a good target for her, as she can deal up to roughly 5x damage to him (with [[Savage Blow]]), and cast a near 100% uptime slow on both him and the [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] featured in [[Baron Seal Strikes/Red Alert 1~20|Red Alert 11~20]].

Overall, Terun's near-100% uptime [[Slow]] is quite nice, though [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rares]] and [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rares]] can usually get the job done as well. She can still find use on enemies that she can outrange and her short recharge time allows you to replace her easily when she is killed. Her 5.7-second attack rate can also prove itself to be handy, as if one of her attacks miss, they won't be tame for long.

==='''True Form'''===
Terun's True Form only grants [[Strong Against]], which may not seem like much, but is very welcome and quite substantial for a boost. Not only does her damage increase by 1.5x-1.8x against her targeted traits, but her survivability is increased too, allowing her to take a few more hits and overall allows her to be stacked more easily. This True Form is less expensive compared to others, making it quite easy to obtain. Her average DPS goes up to 9,400 which is very respectable.

Overall, not a bad True Form if you wish to improve her specialist niche, though using her as a generalist is still questionable due to not improving her stats directly.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Savage Blow''' is quite the substantial buff to her overall DPS, almost as much as '''Attack Buff''' is (around 1.14x). If you truly want to invest in Divine Terun, these two Talents in tandem give her an average DPS of 12,880 against targets at Lv.30. They are top priority without question.

'''[[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]]''' improves her niche against select enemies, the most notable of which are: [[Two Can]], [[Youcan]], [[Berserkory]], [[Elizabeth the LVIth]], and [[Bun Bun Symbiote]]. Despite the presence of Wave Blockers that don't necessitate this Talent to be able to use her against Wave Attack enemies, the extra assurance is always welcome. The insane buffs given by her other Talents also give her decent generalist usage against non-target Wavers too!

Finally, '''[[Barrier Breaker]]''' is entirely unnecessary. Her sheer damage is enough to brute-force most enemy Barriers, save for [[UltraBaaBaa]]'s and Youcan's; against the latter, it can ensure she doesn't throw away an attack or two on its Barrier while you scramble to break it, but the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] can save you that trouble and doesn't rely on a coin flip to activate.

'''HP Buff''' is generally low-priority, since she relies on outranging enemies rather than tanking them. Even in the survivability department, she already has Strong Against to ensure she retains all her repositions.

