==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], She, [[Pegasa (Uber Rare Cat)|Pegasa]], [[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]] and [[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Jeanne]]'s Evolved Forms were missing the ", type" part of their names that other Galaxy Gals had. Version 15.3 also removed "Huntress" from all of Terun's names.
*Terun, Raclesa and Jeanne were the only [[Cyber Academy Galaxy Gals (Gacha Event)|Galaxy Gals]] to have titles in their English names before they were eventually removed.
*Terun may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Artemis|Artemis]], the Greek goddess of the hunt. Artemis, in turn, was associated with the pre-Greek motif [[wikipedia:Potnia Theron|Potnia Theron]], or Mistress of Animals, which is possibly what Terun's name is based on.
**Another possible inspiration for her name could be [[wikipedia:William Tell|William Tell]], an archer from Swiss folklore who's Japanese name reads as ウィリアム・テル (''Wiriamu <u>Teru</u>'').
*The ζ in her Evolved and True Form names is the Greek letter "Zeta".
*The [[Hunting Club (Combo)|Hunting Club]] [[Cat Combo]] implies that [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] is the "best friend who travels with a beast" mentioned in Terun's Japanese description.
**Given that Ururun likely draws inspiration from [[wikia:ghibli:San|San]] from ''[[wikipedia:Princess Mononoke|Princess Mononoke]]'', Terun could be inspired by [[wikia:ghibli:Ashitaka|Ashitaka]]. Her noted calmness, composure, and precision as a hunter, and her portrayal as a prodigy, are similar to Ashitaka's characterization. They both also wield bows.
*Divine Terun ζ's descriptions do not mention her Slow ability, possibly due to character limits.
*Terun does not follow the standard Galaxy Gal design philosophy, as her evolutions become gradually less revealing. This is in a similar vein to [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]].

